==============================================================================
D1  Decentralisation with insurance  (Theorems 6, 7, 8)
==============================================================================
Definition 3 (UM) requires (x*, X*, r*) to solve the agent's problem, with
insurance a CHOICE variable. So the test is: let each agent optimise freely
over physical position AND insurance at prices q, then check its optimal
objective equals the objective at (planner allocation, constructed r).
Degenerate real-time optima make raw allocation distance a poor criterion,
so the objective value is the primary test and allocations are diagnostic.
  [PASS] Eq.(95)  insurance market clears state-by-state   max|sum_k r_k(w)| = 2.910e-10
  [PASS] (UM) planner allocation + constructed transfer is agent-optimal   max relative objective gap = 7.640e-11
  [info] max|DA diff| vs planner = 2.273e+00 (alternative optima; (UM) is settled by the objective test above)
  [PASS] Eq.(94)/(109)  agents' CVaR multipliers equal the planner's   max|gamma_k - gamma| = 5.206e-10

  Control: the same test with Eq. (111)-(112) exactly as printed
  max relative (UM) gap with the printed sign = 9.027e-01
  (a large gap here is the evidence that Eq. 111-112 need r -> -r;
   Eq. 122 in Theorem 9 already uses the corrected sign)

==============================================================================
D4  Heterogeneous confidence levels  (Theorem 9, Eq. 121-123)
==============================================================================
Agents get different beta_k; the planner must use beta_min (Eq. 117-120).
Agents in S_> (beta_k > beta_min) need a CONSTANT insured loss across the
tail (Eq. 121), which the equal-share construction cannot deliver. This
verifies the construction the manuscript flags as not yet proof-checked.
  beta_producers = [0.9, 0.99, 0.99, 0.95, 0.99, 0.99, 0.95, 0.99, 0.99, 0.99]
